{"title":"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Moduli)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Moduli)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Inspecting_the_exponents_of_powers_of_)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Inspecting the exponents of powers of )</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Simple_with_proof)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Simple with proof)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 Proof</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a522f1b44474cef3df06a8a745fec43bde20be0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega = \\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{7} + i \\cdot \\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{7},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2e92550cefae6e71b66ea8a86ac40ebcd6b9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = \\sqrt{-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> Find the value of the product<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926a1478b07a9cae8e5bf2a5d40181beea580ea6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right).\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"51\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_grogg007\">Video solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e-CyXek-ZFs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e-CyXek-ZFs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/51758c369e96208da24bc09c3e3162cf6e52cab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in \\mathbb{Z}, 7\\nmid k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />, we have,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b06d7912504d39a8efae80cf94eea908e959e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp; \\left( \\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1 \\right) \\left( \\omega^{3\\left( 7 - k \\right)} + \\omega^{\\left( 7 - k \\right)} + 1 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\omega^{3 \\cdot 7} + \\omega^{2k + 7} + \\omega^{3k} + \\omega^{-2k + 3 \\cdot 7} + \\omega^7 + \\omega^k + \\omega^{3\\left( 7 - k \\right)} + \\omega^{\\left( 7 - k \\right)} + 1 \\\\ &amp; = 1 + \\omega^{2k} + \\omega^{3k} + \\omega^{-2k} + 1 + \\omega^k + \\omega^{-3k} + \\omega^{-k} + 1 \\\\ &amp; = 2 + \\omega^{-3k} \\sum_{j=0}^6 \\omega^{j k} \\\\ &amp; = 2 + \\omega^{-3k} \\frac{1 - \\omega^{7 k}}{1 - \\omega^k} \\\\ &amp; = 2 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"510\" height=\"210\" />\nThe second and the fifth equalities follow from the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97fe07f32eccdb7fe3c97421f32623ad620b3f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^7 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2cb4058de6e84ffa962bf4b6f57fa5e3723bc0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\Pi_{k=0}^6 \\left( \\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1 \\right) &amp; = \\left( \\omega^{3 \\cdot 0} + \\omega^0 + 1 \\right) \\Pi_{k=1}^3 \\left( \\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1 \\right) \\left( \\omega^{3\\left( 7 - k \\right)} + \\omega^{\\left( 7 - k \\right)} + 1 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 3 \\cdot 2^3 \\\\ &amp; = \\boxed{\\textbf{024}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"634\" height=\"79\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, otherwise the first equation would equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ~inaccessibles\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Moduli.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Moduli)\">Solution 2 (Moduli)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Moduli)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the answer must be a positive integer, it is just equal to the modulus of the product. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b650ca6e4aee08b6fea7ad21b17b0efd34d4a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_n = \\left(\\textrm{cis }\\frac{2n\\pi}{7}\\right)^3 + \\textrm{cis }\\frac{2n\\pi}{7} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"249\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Then, our product is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b6367decd6d31ba0eaae3b0d768f65edb05026.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|z_0||z_1||z_2||z_3||z_4||z_5||z_6|.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d853a9f39815c8b07e9cbc8f346c00117ced0636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, and we may observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13ec3386d628b5ca8d96ff83af9b240831084348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/6549fc05b6f412c0869e79ac0aa81306b2f15c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{7-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> are conjugates for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, meaning that their magnitudes are the same. Thus, our product is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195e814255c0688f4ee558ac79c87990d3a6cc93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3|z_1|^2|z_2|^2|z_3|^2\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67ad4a9fcad5621f9c659acc10edd73cd72a8f82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 3\\left((\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 1)^2 + (\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + \\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{7})^2\\right) \\left((\\cos \\frac{12\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + 1)^2 + (\\sin \\frac{12\\pi}{7} + \\sin \\frac{4\\pi}{7})^2\\right) \\left((\\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + 1)^2 + (\\sin \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{7})^2\\right)\\]\" width=\"1158\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Let us simplify the first term. Expanding, we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31b35025f7bff7c3754e56ebee823c5b42d6704.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos^2 \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + \\cos^2 \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 1 + 2\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 2\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + 2\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\sin^2 \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + \\sin^2 \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 2\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{7}.\\]\" width=\"716\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Rearranging and cancelling, we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334f34090504689723e82b29798f79e3f587de64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 + 2\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + 2\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 2\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 2\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{7}.\\]\" width=\"460\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>By the cosine subtraction formula, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2422c80016ebf45a38c68e2280da6a705a9c62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + 2\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{7} = \\cos \\frac{6\\pi - 2\\pi}{7} = \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"450\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the first term is equivalent to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/67048ca68ac68de4e9aa345857d43f53394d222b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 + 2(\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7}).\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, the second and third terms are, respectively, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010cf1ef33f36799ca677f1ea24039fc2dda5b37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 + 2(\\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{8\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{12\\pi}{7}),\\textrm{ and}\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/051ce78f9e2054332ea4ec4f2078d7eb1425e5ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 + 2(\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{12\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7}).\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Next, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f7832f397bbdb22a10e435e1ee1308bdcd701399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"38\" />. This is because\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c190478cd3dcafe80a9b01852525f493a5168c59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7} = \\frac{1}{2}(\\textrm{cis }\\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\textrm{cis }\\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\textrm{cis }\\frac{6\\pi}{7} + \\textrm{cis }\\frac{8\\pi}{7} + \\textrm{cis }\\frac{10\\pi}{7} + \\textrm{cis }\\frac{12\\pi}{7})\\]\" width=\"610\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6ca330947378348178c14eb17267d8780ed988.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{2}(-1)\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ea48af299072521b37850db6f6fe84f77e6c5fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= -\\frac{1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the first term is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3578052075cc698812ba5debf3ffe30360ca37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x = \\cos 2\\pi - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" />, so therefore the second and third terms can both also be simplified to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/55650f0467ad0591a289070da36a3e40282a8840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 2(\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7}) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"289\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, our answer is simply\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc458fdfa790fb23549cbeb3ed925cd39bfcbecb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c240dff0653b28d4e87f539a01a92467d3859f4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\boxed{\\mathbf{024}}.\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy100\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Inspecting_the_exponents_of_powers_of_.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Inspecting_the_exponents_of_powers_of_)\">Solution 3 (Inspecting the exponents of powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Inspecting the exponents of powers of )\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We write out the product in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5e17866a772e5e80d894475e9c44b83710d92e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right)=3(\\omega^3+\\omega+1)(\\omega^6+\\omega^2+1)(\\omega^9+\\omega^3+1)(\\omega^{12}+\\omega^4+1)(\\omega^{15}+\\omega^5+1)(\\omega^{18}+\\omega^6+1).\\]\" width=\"734\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Grouping the terms in the following way exploits the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc4ab063e58b07ddc4c82a325442b9a2789dc90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^{7k}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> for an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, when multiplying out two adjacent products from left to right:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eef005d2d9ee576f362fe4d233f31e29d7d98db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3} \\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right)=(\\omega^3+\\omega+1)(\\omega^{18}+\\omega^6+1)(\\omega^6+\\omega^2+1)(\\omega^{15}+\\omega^5+1)(\\omega^9+\\omega^3+1)(\\omega^{12}+\\omega^4+1).\\]\" width=\"740\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWhen multiplying two numbers with like bases, we add the exponents. We can now rewrite the exponents of each product (two at a time, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is treated as the identity) as a series of arrays: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a2531941a2234546e80d51d3eeba61a23c17c544.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(A)}\\begin{bmatrix} 3&amp;1 &amp;0 \\\\ 18&amp;6&amp;0\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc428bd48490e9642c75f9bc916c1da5ed78402.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(B)}\\begin{bmatrix} 6&amp;2 &amp;0 \\\\ 15&amp;5&amp;0\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/5913ff57931f2b19177e0cfb65c7398d131254c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(C)}\\begin{bmatrix} 9&amp;3 &amp;0 \\\\ 12&amp;4&amp;0\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13bd26889155d1a0abb8d24f89c9781bc5f98ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega=e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" />. When raising <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> to a power, the numerator of the fraction is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times whatever power <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is raised to, multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b8140b36626ce2471bee5976512d8d89ced83740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi i$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />. Since the period of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc379f1d29bfe042429197991830e1ec03210800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> we multiply each array by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> then reduce each entry <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d740eade56f9fded14cb2f9f7a4faf66fd8a7363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod{14},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> as each entry in an array represents an exponent which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is raised to.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b466c8cb3f95f53aed088dc09df06112b04a3440.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(A)}\\begin{bmatrix} 6&amp;2 &amp;0 \\\\ 8&amp;12&amp;0\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907c93b39d1a95fab42435b3a3d89ba315110cdc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(B)}\\begin{bmatrix} 12&amp;4 &amp;0 \\\\ 2&amp;10&amp;0\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028d39223481c05bb916dfab2e6960b1ccca128e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(C)}\\begin{bmatrix} 4&amp;6 &amp;0 \\\\ 10&amp;8&amp;0\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>To obtain the correct exponents, we seperately add each element of the lower row to one element of the top row. \n</p><p>Therefore (after reducing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde18d2796cf32ed7d8de6ee6737d1fa44a93d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> again), we get the following sets: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/88138b6f17795b22ebd7d1e222a8a5279a4a1b15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\{0, 4, 6, 10, 0, 2, 8, 12, 0\\}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad88cbb2efdbe7d2909a96aacc34ef4e0da83387.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\{0, 8, 12, 6, 0, 4, 2, 10, 0\\}\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa4d26369fa32bdad887dc5593faa4c56046113.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\{0, 12, 4, 2, 0, 8, 10, 8, 0\\}.\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Raising <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> to the power of each element in every set then multiplying over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d384e7cea1a848fce02b68a8bc4d4bbb333e2ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}, \\textbf{(B)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> yields \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd128754c66af1fceabebf079af1caf2bded356.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3} \\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right)=\\left(\\sum_{a\\in \\textbf{(A)}} \\omega^a\\right)\\left(\\sum_{b\\in \\textbf{(B)}} \\omega^b\\right)\\left(\\sum_{c\\in \\textbf{(C)}} \\omega^c\\right)\\]\" width=\"457\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b2d9b1189b05c2ae5bf29ec2a5c76f3d93f56e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(\\sum_{a\\in \\textbf{(A)}} \\omega^a\\right)^3\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"67\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b1ce01b7e90a7557d650d25fa1438798ec98ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(\\omega^0+\\omega^4+\\omega^6+\\omega^{10}+\\omega^0+\\omega^2+\\omega^8+\\omega^{12}+\\omega^0\\right)^3\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0e5db7fd803aa9198c70aa869105ed2f9cbdf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(3+\\omega^2+\\omega^4+\\omega^6+\\omega^8+\\omega^{10}+\\omega^{12}\\right)^3,\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"24\" />\nas these sets are all identical. \n</p><p>Summing as a geometric series, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948c024f902e4db59e9fc2e881dd0e27d7bcf30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3} \\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right)=\\left(3+\\frac{\\omega^2(\\omega^{12}-1)}{\\omega^2-1}\\right)^3\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e007302012241d011d5f34f38a5252d90f0012.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(3+\\frac{\\omega^{14}-\\omega^2}{\\omega^2-1}\\right)^3\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07dbd73869860619fd7c211fe5761a1bc89eac00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(3+\\frac{1-\\omega^2}{\\omega^2-1}\\right)^3\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283ffb41e278fa74160d6ace2bb34925ca8801c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(3-1)^3=8.\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23ab25f6ee0f51a3171197dd01bee3decfb05d1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3} \\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right)=8,\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"51\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/43679d62e189799187a74552600ae79b0d398cbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=0}^6 \\left(\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1\\right)=3\\cdot8=\\boxed{\\textbf{(024)}}.\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6baa4fcac2715b9deb1379a1c247bbf205857b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-r)(1-s)(1-t)(w-r)(w-s)(w-t)(w^2-r)(w^2-s)(w^2-t)....(w^6-r)(w^6-s)(w^6-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"747\" height=\"21\" />, (treat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb58083eb8d4d62eb681f4ed034466167364aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254b00de0340e532c68728c5f4eb6c365cd84b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+x+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> then k varies from 0 to 6.\n</p><p><br />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa7e4dae453f67aa78269d730f7cae70296659a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,s,t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" /> are the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254b00de0340e532c68728c5f4eb6c365cd84b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+x+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nThis is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a606000268109a1e9122356365bc3f7052ad9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(r^7-1)(s^7-1)(t^7-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d55882002d00a8a8caa80b6b0b86d188dce33e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r^7-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0f5908f8fd441e050d88bc1d79d25d86efb7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-1)(r-w)(r-w^2)...(r-w^6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"21\" /> share the same roots and leading coefficient so are thus the same polynomial. \n</p><p><br />\nTo find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a606000268109a1e9122356365bc3f7052ad9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(r^7-1)(s^7-1)(t^7-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p><p><br />\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1defe916891318f4c003c6532643b38f756aeb11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r^7-1)=(r-1)(r^6+r^5+r^4+r^3+r^2+r+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"21\" />. Since r satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254b00de0340e532c68728c5f4eb6c365cd84b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+x+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c32457c1f355779eac0a698cf0a13bb40c17249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^6+r^4+r^3=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p><br />\nSubstituting, you are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e497682c78085f208eaf77103f2d2f96d3d960f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^5+r^2+r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d3ac0cc2263cbbfc6ed418dd3ebc9c6a0c571f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2(r^3+1)+r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"21\" />, and after repeatedly substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3d9615b5e10e2b093caa0e76be79026bb895cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3+r+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> you are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/2802da708cc379201510b2e564cb27873a4b401b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2r^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nSo now the problem is reduced to finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a259dfccbf504a8056b878fcee95a86347e93a55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(r-1)(s-1)(t-1)(-2r^3)(-2s^3)(-2t^3)=8(rst)^3(r-1)(s-1)(t-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"573\" height=\"21\" />, and vietas gives you the result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d2cca89d5aa7ed0a9130ce403b8bf8a23a869c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> -resources\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c06e883e0ce5dd4f2db77978983b421faeba82c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\omega^0+\\omega^0+1)(\\omega^3+\\omega+1)(\\omega^6+\\omega^2+1)(\\omega^9+\\omega^3+1)\\\\(\\omega^{12}+\\omega^4+1)(\\omega^{15}+\\omega^5+1)(\\omega^{18}+\\omega^6+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>The key here then is noticing that cis<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/9001eb054b969f03662d4d373351d956b94ab485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>From this we realize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d34d7074283348e727817b6655cd6bf653a196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^{7n+a}=\\omega^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a residue<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d96b7fc4a61b03f47d647dc26b5bd2fdf80232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod 7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Our expression then simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed048845108c245210c20814e110bcc01a53ccbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)(\\omega^3+\\omega+1)(\\omega^6+\\omega^2+1)(\\omega^2+\\omega^3+1)\\\\(\\omega^5+\\omega^4+1)(\\omega+\\omega^5+1)(\\omega^4+\\omega^6+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The key then becomes multiplying the 2nd and 7th, 3rd and 6th, 4th and 5th terms because they would result in a couple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c88ec146103349491e0e513c8bcd72c6f26df7d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> which will cancel out.\n</p><p>Multiplying them you obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf6d15a09fa3a6e98b8c2aa79716b0de8aedba79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^6+\\omega^5+\\omega^4+\\omega^3+\\omega^2+\\omega+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />. Recognizing this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a729aba4257d431a1d3b51fe9c738788ca964d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\omega^7-1}{\\omega-1}+2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"42\" /> For terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217a2c8f341cf8e3d1f342ef6f3964b4f3e6eef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*7, 3*6, 4*5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/75444b3d508062c01ea30f97427406a33b5c84a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^7-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> (cis<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/9001eb054b969f03662d4d373351d956b94ab485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />) We are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f3581d37dc6b11eb2d759170db79de58a80b6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)(2)(2)(2)=\\boxed{024}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"163\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~BigBrain_2009\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Simple_with_proof.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Simple_with_proof)\">Solution 6 (Simple with proof)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Simple with proof)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let \\( x = \\omega^k \\). Let \\( \\alpha_1 \\), \\( \\alpha_2 \\), and \\( \\alpha_3 \\) be the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + x + 1 \\). Thus, the product simplifies down to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4fbb1175a4f7c6d8ea088f66399b1c8d2cd5cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=0}^6 (x - \\alpha_1)(x - \\alpha_2)(x - \\alpha_3)\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"51\" />\nReturn \\( x \\) as the value \\( \\omega^k \\). It becomes evident that every \\( \\omega^k \\) is also a 7th root of unity. Thus, because each product cycles between the seven roots of unity, one can rewrite the entirety of the product as \\( -(\\alpha_1^7 - 1)(\\alpha_2^7 - 1)(\\alpha_3^7 - 1) \\). Through Vieta's, \\( \\alpha_1 \\alpha_2 \\alpha_3 = -1 \\), and through <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton%27s_Sums\" title=\"Newton&#39;s Sums\">Newton's Sums</a>, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5fac6b03aa9ec71760a3b8c75901d75e7e9d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_Proof\">Solution 6 Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The most likely confusion point is: how do we get from simplifying the product into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/264611533458384afcb0796bfbd7f58f8681fd0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-\\alpha_1)(x-\\alpha_2)(x-\\alpha_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" /> into immediately concluding that the product is essentially <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf16649716b4e8dee0dadaf60c224bcb52570db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(\\alpha_1^7-1)(\\alpha_2^7-1)(\\alpha_3^7-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"21\" />?\n</p><p>We can prove this quite easily.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th root of unity, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcf3d01a7c6f1b61d5217c168af1ccd5973e9f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33ca66e2665479ad0b9d8526fb30631f868fbcf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851728412576532a926a083e9f204ca677fb92d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)(a-x)(a-x^2) \\cdots (a-x^{n-1}) \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"301\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>For each term in the product, factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in each product to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0ad33b54febfe9a0e33fa07d7b3550a1fb70887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^{n}\\cdot (1-a)(x-a)(x^2-a)(x^3-a)(...)(x^{n-1}-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"412\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f0f830b5b25ea929198068e407e8c9f62f56c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, we have the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e50528189caec92350335db768080f94fa754c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^{7} = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now, note that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> term is a root of unity! This is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and that must correspond to some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> power. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is also a root of unity! Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must also be a root of unity. Then, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f0f830b5b25ea929198068e407e8c9f62f56c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, our final rewritten form is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3df69d80a2d32917b7ef95b3c841305ec2ab3a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(a^7-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>So, for our case\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Power of Logic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/o6w9t43GpJs?si=aoe-uM3m5AIwpz_H\">https://youtu.be/o6w9t43GpJs?si=aoe-uM3m5AIwpz_H</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II\" title=\"2023 AIME II\">2023 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022459\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.090 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.116 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 728/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 26757/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.044      1 -total\n 57.98%    8.722      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.71%    5.824      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23918:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022459 and revision id 287972. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}